                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a game play loop where you kill zombies and loot. That's actually it. The loop is like a 1/10 for most probably less but for those who love killing zombies 3/10. \n\nThe problem is the endgame where everything is stupidly expensive for example you get this \"broken key\" it cost a Mil to turn it into a key for a loot box for a non existing chance of good gear, yes like gatcha game but the reward doesn't really pay off. The problem is how long it takes to get to that mil. Ammo at most I've sold was a stack of rifle ammo for 6k. Investing in good gear fair enough something we all have to do. \n\nNow events I've seen they're just repeats of what ever slop they did last year but made it harder and worse for casuals. New items to craft cost 400/500 tokens where you do public zones 10/20 or maybe event 25! and that's every 20 minutes. For casual players who only have one character good luck getting older weapons and gear as they cost 5000 tokens and 1mil per item. Now lets talk about the event bosses I think the developers are deaf because they scream in you ear like you don't have eardrums to damage. They didn't even consider the kind of damage they do to people outside of the game.\n\nHonestly, it's the community that makes this game but the devs don't actually care about new/casual players. I am trying to get into endgame more but I wish it was like 10-25% easier for events as these are what can pull in new players.  \n\nSeeing a lot of bans from devs not for cheating but for calling out the devs for their flaws and not liking their Ideas is bad!!!! You'll find a lot on reddit and other posts about their ego problem. I got banned on their discussion for \"trolling\" when all I have done was tell people exactly what I've said here. Honestly with Devs like this don't spend money just F2P it's not actually worth supporting people with ego problems and refuse to better the game. My justification for this is the fact that they haven't introduce anything worth while or new and all events are the same stuff but harder. If you are a new player with 0 alts good luck. This game was \"fun\" but becoming a chore means it's your second job. Even Vets are fucking tired of their slop but because they are dreaming/hoping the devs get their head out of their asses and actually do some shit.",
